# `read_json(..., infer_rows = n)`: raising `infer_rows` widens a late type change to `arrow.json`,
# and a column that is all `null` in the sample infers `arrow.json` and accepts objects past
# `infer_rows`.
mode: run
---- query
from read_json('../../data/json/late_type.ndjson', infer_rows = 3) | sort by id asc;
from read_json('../../data/json/late_null_obj.ndjson', infer_rows = 1) | sort by id asc
---- expected
id   | n
long | dynamic
-----+--------
   1 | 1
   2 | 2
   3 | "oops"

id   | extra
long | dynamic
-----+--------
   1 | null
   2 | {"k":1}
